title: The Heavens Declare – Creation and the Creator
description: Creation and the Creator: the heavens declare the glory of God and leave all men without excuse, all creation is a parable, a literal six day creation about 6,000 years ago, evolution the worship of time, and the gap theory of Scofield and Ruckman refuted, from the teachings on creation.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-creation.html
highlight: creat; heaven; earth

# One deck for the doctrine "Creation" (21 teachings), its themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
--- The Heavens Declare [title]
overline: Doctrine · Creation
heading: The Heavens Declare
sub: Creation and the Creator, a literal creation, and all creation as a parable of God.
refs: Genesis 1:1; Psalms 19:1; Romans 1:20; Exodus 20:11; Job 38:4
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 6474
--- In the beginning
big: Genesis 1:1 | mark: In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth
p: The fullness of the Godhead exists when nothing else did, including time, and through Him was created light, substance, life, and mankind. Everything after its own kind, with the seed contained therein propagating that life over time.
p: From Genesis 1 through Revelation 22, the Bible is the story of Jesus Christ. God revealing His Son to us that we may believe and have eternal life.

=== Creation declares God's glory
# from 17735
--- The heavens declare the glory of God
kicker: Creation declares God's glory
big: Psalms 19:1-3 | mark: The heavens declare the glory of God; There is no speech nor language, where their voice is not heard
p: Looking upon the night sky we see His precision and power. The things of creation speak without words, that all man may understand. They don't need a language. They don't need to be explained.
p: The vain hypothetical of a savage on a remote island, never hearing the gospel, is undone by the understanding that all nature is a parable and a testament of God, showing men truth.

# from 10676, 17735
--- Without excuse
kicker: Creation declares God's glory
big: Romans 1:20 | mark: the invisible things of him from the creation of the world are clearly seen; so that they are without excuse
p: Nature teaches us God's law. His wrath is revealed against those who sin, even without the oracles of God. Man can see the law of God, know it written in their hearts, watch the outcome of their behavior, and know they are guilty.
p: If the day declares His righteousness and the night His knowledge, and the very nature of things speaks to His wrath, then the oracles of God give us the hope of His mercy.

# from 10676
--- The creature more than the Creator
kicker: Creation declares God's glory
big: Romans 1:25 | mark: worshipped and served the creature more than the Creator
p: Men knowing the judgment and wrath of God made up stories to explain it. Devised complex systems of works and worship of idols to justify their sin.
p: They change the glory of an uncorruptible God into images made like unto corruptible man, like the Catholic church or the Orthodox that split off it. Or like unto birds and animals and creeping things. Worship of nature. Worship of themselves even.

# from 17032
--- The cornerstone laid
kicker: Creation declares God's glory
big: Job 38:4 | mark: Where wast thou when I laid the foundations of the earth?
p: The foundations of the world are set by Him, and the corner stone thereof ([[Job 38:6-7]]). The morning stars sang together, and the sons of God shouted for joy and the truth of Jesus Christ, the lamb slain before the foundation of the world. The cornerstone laid, upon Which all is built.
p: Time itself is a testimony of His power. The day chasing away the darkness.

# from 17039, 17040
--- Job asks why, God shows Who
kicker: Creation declares God's glory
big: Job 39:26 | mark: Doth the hawk fly by thy wisdom
p: The wild goat, the wild ass, the unicorn (not a mythical beast, but the wild ox), the ostrich, the horse, the hawk and the eagle. Not by will of man. In all this, man is helpless. It is all the providence of God.
p: Like these wild creatures, we wander in stubborn liberty, yet God sustains us in mercy. Job is asking “why?” But God is showing him “Who.”

# from 16895, 16972
--- Ask now the beasts
kicker: Creation declares God's glory
big: Job 12:9 | mark: the hand of the LORD hath wrought this
p: *Ask now the beasts, and they shall teach thee* ([[Job 12:7]]). God reveals Himself to man in innumerable ways. Every man knows God is real, and all creation testifies of His wrath and nature and truth.
p: The stars in the heavens, the earth in space, the oceans and land that bound the waters, all speak of His power and glory. These are just a glimpse; *the thunder of his power who can understand?* ([[Job 26:14]])
read: app:doctrine-creation~17735 | The heavens declare the glory of God
read: app:doctrine-creation~10676 | The wrath of God revealed from heaven

=== Creation is the parable
# from 3354, 17737
--- Creation is the parable
kicker: Creation is the parable
big: Psalms 19:5 | mark: Which is as a bridegroom coming out of his chamber
p: It's not that parables use creation to explain God's word. Creation *is* the parable. It exists to illustrate the biblical truth. Not the other way around.
p: Every seed we sow, every shooting star, bird in flight, or wave crashing on the shore. All creation is a parable to those with ears to hear and eyes to see. The boldness of the sun breaking forth in the morning is as the risen Christ.

# from 4412
--- Children of the day
kicker: Creation is the parable
big: 1 Thessalonians 5:5 | mark: Ye are all the children of light, and the children of the day
p: One of the reasons God created day and night, if not the only reason, is a picture of the end. On the day of the Lord, the damned get darkness. We are of the day and of the light. When we hear God's word say it, we can picture it, and in picturing it understand what God's saying.
p: We are to be as the firmament, as the rising sun and the crashing wave. New creatures in Christ, brought forth as a testimony to God's greatness.

# from 17556
--- Two trees in Eden
kicker: Creation is the parable
big: Genesis 2:9 | mark: the tree of life also in the midst of the garden, and the tree of knowledge of good and evil
p: From the beginning God gave two options to the man He had created: the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, the law, and the tree of life, which is by faith in the word of God.

# from 3785
--- The birds were gleaning
kicker: Creation is the parable
big: Deuteronomy 25:4 | mark: Thou shalt not muzzle the ox when he treadeth out the corn
p: The same birds who all year kept the harmful bugs away from my garden were feasting on my peas. I had set traps for a chipmunk. As I prayed, God said to me, “they're gleaning.” The Spirit bringing all things into remembrance. A laborer gets its reward.
p: And, just like that, my frustration disappeared. This is God's garden.

# from 6606
--- While the earth remaineth
kicker: Creation is the parable
big: Genesis 8:22 | mark: While the earth remaineth, seedtime and harvest; shall not cease
p: God vows never to destroy every living thing because of the evil imagination of man's heart. Rather than curse the ground, God vows to preserve the world as is until the end.
p: This is why environmentalist panic is unbiblical nonsense. We are not going to see cataclysmic climate change of any type before the day of the Lord.
read: app:doctrine-creation~3354 | Creation is the parable
read: app:doctrine-creation~3785 | The birds were gleaning

=== A literal creation
# from 6474
--- In six days
kicker: Literal creation, a young earth
big: Exodus 20:11 | mark: For in six days the LORD made heaven and earth
p: This is a literal story of creation. Not because of fossils found in weird places, or the problems with carbon dating, or the complexity and variance of life. But because God said this is how it happened. The God who cannot lie tells us these things and that they are so.
p: You don't have to believe in the literal creation in order to believe on Jesus. But it is difficult to express that faith to others while doubting much of His word, or thinking it allegory.

# from 6474, 6382
--- Evolution, the worship of time
kicker: Literal creation, a young earth
big: 1 Timothy 6:20 | mark: oppositions of science falsely so called
p: Evolution, which is the worship of time, or Kronos as the creator, is literally the worship of the created, because God created time. And so we know it's false.
p: Biblical creation explains the kinds and types, incredible beauty, the complexity of systems, and gives us a true accounting of the origin of race and nations. Nonbelievers have faith in science falsely so called, the theories of Jews and Masons and Jesuits that tickle their ears.

# from 6557, 14678
--- The chronogenealogies
kicker: Literal creation, a young earth
big: Luke 3:38 | mark: which was the son of Adam, which was the son of God
p: The ages of Genesis 5 are given literally: 1,558 years from Adam to Shem, about 2,008 years from Adam to Abraham, and roughly 2,000 more to Christ. This places the earth at just slightly more than 6,000 years old. Give or take a century or two.
p: The Septuagint's chronology has Methuselah living years after the Flood. The calendar is not the preserved word of God, but the genealogies are there to mark time.

# from 3653
--- Primary doctrine and opinions
kicker: Literal creation, a young earth
big: 2 Timothy 2:15 | mark: rightly dividing the word of truth
p: Literal creation is a primary doctrine. Biblical age as determined by generations is secondary. A precise number of years has Biblical basis, but is incidental, and people of good faith can disagree.
p: Don't project your opinions of the worldly onto scripture and become dogmatic in things that are ultimately not important.
read: app:doctrine-creation~6474 | A literal creation about 6,000 years ago
read: app:doctrine-creation~6557 | The chronogenealogies and a young earth

=== The gap theory refuted
# from 11607, 16228
--- Scofield's gap
kicker: The gap theory refuted
big: Genesis 1:2 | mark: And the earth was without form, and void
p: Scofield interrupts God's creation to invent a “gap” between verse 1 and verse 2: millions or billions of years, a pre-Adamic world destroyed, “proved” by Jeremiah's vision ([[Jeremiah 4:23-26]]). Made to match the geologists of his era. Ruckman taught it too.
p: If he is inventing things in the first verse of the first chapter, why do they trust anything else he wrote? How about the world conform to the word of God?

# from 6522
--- Very good
kicker: The gap theory refuted
big: Genesis 1:31 | mark: behold, it was very good
p: When God looks at His creation after His work was done, He found it was “very good.” Perfect. Complete. Not *very good, other than the botched world and fallen angels*.
p: Satan is a created being. There was a day Satan was created ([[Ezekiel 28:15]]). Some believe the devil is a balance to God, or the Mormons say Jesus' brother. These are blasphemous statements. Satan is a creature; Jesus the Creator.

# from 16228
--- Adam knew Eve
kicker: The gap theory refuted
big: Genesis 4:1 | mark: Adam knew Eve his wife; and she conceived, and bare Cain
p: Ruckman taught the serpent seed: that Satan fathered Cain by Eve. Cain was Adam's son according to the word of God. Making him a literal child of Satan removes the entire point of free will and faith in the story.
p: False teachers bait the hook with some truth, then reel folks in with absolute nonsense. Sheep's clothing.
read: app:doctrine-creation~11607 | Scofield's gap theory from Jeremiah 4
read: app:doctrine-creation~6522 | Satan was created, and the gap theory is false
read: app:doctrine-creation~16228 | Ruckmanism: serpent seed and the Gap Theory

=== The law of the LORD
--- The Law of the LORD [title]
overline: Creation
heading: Converting the Soul
big: Psalms 19:7 | mark: The law of the LORD is perfect, converting the soul
center: The heavens declare His glory, and in that knowledge, we find His word, and from that word, salvation.
